  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Change icon color",
      "text": "Use `iconColor` prop to change icon color. You can reference colors from `theme.colors` or use any valid CSS color:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Indeterminate state",
      "text": "`Checkbox` supports indeterminate state. When `indeterminate` prop is set,\n`checked` prop is ignored (checkbox always has checked styles):\n\n  data={CheckboxDemos.indeterminate}\n  demoProps={{ toggle: true }}\n/>",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Checkbox with tooltip",
      "text": "You can change target element to which tooltip is attached with `refProp`:\n\n- If `refProp` is not set, the tooltip is attached to the checkbox input\n- If `refProp=\"rootRef\"` is set, the tooltip is attached to the root element (contains label, input and other elements)",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pointer cursor",
      "text": "By default, checkbox input and label have `cursor: default` (same as native `input[type=\"checkbox\"]`).\nTo change cursor to pointer, set `cursorType` on [theme](/theming/theme-object/):",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Add custom sizes",
      "text": "You can add any number of custom sizes with [data-size](/styles/data-attributes/) attribute:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Checkbox.Indicator",
      "text": "`Checkbox.Indicator` looks exactly the same as `Checkbox` component, but it does not\nhave any semantic meaning, it's just a visual representation of checkbox state. You\ncan use it in any place where you need to display checkbox state without any interaction\nrelated to the indicator. For example, it is useful in cards based on buttons, trees, etc.\n\nNote that `Checkbox.Indicator` cannot be focused or selected with keyboard. It is not\naccessible and should not be used as a replacement for `Checkbox` component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Checkbox.Card component",
      "text": "`Checkbox.Card` component can be used as a replacement for `Checkbox` to build custom\ncards/buttons/other things that work as checkboxes. The root element of the component\nhas `role=\"checkbox\"` attribute, it is accessible by default and supports the same\nkeyboard interactions as `input[type=\"checkbox\"]`.\n\nYou can use `Checkbox.Card` with `Checkbox.Group` the same way as `Checkbox` component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "Set `aria-label` or `label` prop to make the checkbox accessible:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
